use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Announcement import Announcement
from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation

export ui-component DateInput:
    description:
        A date input lets the user type a date into separate segments for the
        day, month and year, laid out in the order and with the separators
        that are usual for their locale. It has no calendar.

    behaviors:
        - @{FormParticipation}
        - @{Announcement}

    value:
        A plain calendar date, with no time of day and no time zone, as with a
        DatePicker. It only has a value once every segment is filled in. Until
        then the value is empty, though the segments keep what was typed.

    segments:
        Each segment shows its part of the date, or a placeholder such as "dd",
        "mm" or "yyyy" while it is empty. Whether the month can be shown as a
        name, and whether leading zeros are shown, follows the user's locale
        unless the component says otherwise.

    typing:
        Typing digits fills the focused segment. Focus moves on to the next
        segment by itself once the segment is full, or as soon as no further
        digit could make sense, so typing 4 in the month moves straight on.
        Only digits that could make sense are accepted.

    keyboard:
        Left and Right move between segments. Up and Down raise and lower the
        focused segment by one, going round within that segment, so December
        goes up to January without changing the year. Page Up and Page Down
        move by a bigger amount. Home and End go to the segment's lowest and
        highest value. Backspace clears the focused segment, or moves back to
        the one before if it is already empty. Whether each segment is its own
        stop in the Tab order is up to the chosen library.

    pasting:
        Pasting a whole date fills every segment at once, if the pasted text
        can be read as a date.

    limits:
        The component can set an earliest and latest date, and mark other days
        as unavailable. A date outside them can still be typed, but it is
        marked as not valid rather than silently changed.

    range:
        For a range, there are two sets of segments, one for the start and one
        for the end, each with its own name.

    accessibility:
        The whole date input has a name, and each segment has its own, such as
        "month". Assistive tools read out each segment's new value as it
        changes, without focus moving.

    disabled:
        A disabled date input can't be focused or changed. A read-only one can
        be focused and read out, but not changed.

    nonGoals:
        - No calendar. A date input with a calendar is a DatePicker
        - No time of day. That's a TimePicker
        - Whether segments can be left out, such as the day for a card's expiry
            month, is up to the chosen library
